--- 8. Already right - leave alone ---
ACES + `outputColorSpace = SRGBColorSpace` with a HalfFloat, `samples: 4` composer RT and `antialias:false` on the canvas, `OutputPass` after bloom/bokeh and SMAA + the grade (grain/vignette/AB) in tone-mapped space: correct order and the right MSAA placement. PCFSoft + `bias -0.0006` + `normalBias 0.028` with a tank-following sun is a sound choice - do not add a second shadow-casting light. PMREM of the same equirect sky used for `background`, with `sunVector()` driving both the sky's sun blob and the DirectionalLight, is the right single-source-of-truth structure: keep it and only touch its elevation/azimuth constants. For a photo look, keep the sun at 22-28 deg elevation and 95-120 deg of horizontal separation from the camera azimuth — back-lit the shadow hides behind the tank, front-lit the sand and hull flatten; side-lit gives a shadow inside the frame and a lit visible flank. 94 links/side on a closed curve, the lathe/normal fixes and the roughnessMap-driven armour are all worth keeping as-is.

